      <title>Dozens of court cases in England and Wales affected by undisclosed AI use in 2026</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/26/dozens-of-court-cases-in-england-and-wales-affected-by-undisclosed-ai-use-in-2026</link>
      <description>Exclusive: Investigation finds at least 25 cases affected by AI-generated witness statements, fictitious case law and nonexistent statutes Undisclosed AI use has affected more than two dozen court cases this year, prompting judges to complain about AI-generated witness statements, fictitious case law and nonexistent statutes, an investigation has revealed. Proceedings where judges have been forced to deal with lawyers, police officers and claimants misusing the technology in 2026 include a…</description>
