      <title>I’m an AI leader at a tech giant. Our industry has stopped taking safety seriously | Anonymous</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/nov/26/ai-leader-tech-giant-trust-safeguarding-privacy-profit</link>
      <description>We’re developing the most powerful tech in history – but trust, safeguarding and privacy are being sidelined in favour of huge profit I’m a senior AI leader at one of the world’s biggest tech companies, and the products we put out into the world are increasingly being recklessly rushed, without proper consideration. The tech industry used to take safety and privacy seriously, but lately I have become worried by how rash we have become. In a sector that is obsessed with being first, ethical…</description>
