      <title>Employers: do you have concerns about the rollout of Muse and other AI agents?</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/26/employers-do-you-have-concerns-about-the-rollout-of-muse-and-other-ai-agents</link>
      <description>Are you worried about staff connecting their digital assistants to work emails and databases? What steps are you taking to address this? Meta has rolled out its Muse AI assistant, which can be tasked with shopping, booking tickets and carrying out negotiations on a user’s behalf, across countries including the UK, US, Canada, Australia and Japan. The AI agent needs the customer’s permission to go out and make purchases, connect to apps, use bank details or send emails autonomously. However…</description>
