      <title>Elon Musk pledges to give two SpaceX shares to every child in the US</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/26/elon-musk-pledges-to-give-two-spacex-shares-to-every-child-in-the-us</link>
      <description>The total value of the shares could reach almost $18bn and comes as tech companies debate how to share the spoils of the AI boom Elon Musk, the world’s richest person, has pledged to give every child in the US two shares in SpaceX, the space ⁠and AI company he ​runs, worth a total of almost $18bn. In a brief post on X, the social media platform that he owns, Musk said children will receive one share from the company itself, and one from him personally. SpaceX announced earlier on Wednesday…</description>
